  "source_blocks": [
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00012_1e7eb292cce1",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "Unheaded source preface",
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "source_text": "<!--@0¶3-->\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td><strong>CANONICAL PREMISE<br />\n</strong>Core Species traits are not faction bonuses layered onto identical parties. They arise from the physical composition of the expedition party and alter which constraints the party can absorb: Mouse distributes bodies and personal items, Squirrel extends material capacity at risk of shedding, and Rabbit extends Field movement according to the Rabbit share of the party.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00036_078e41d768e0",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "1. Design Doctrine",
      "block_type": "table_row",
      "source_text": "| Squirrel    | 1 Squirrel = 1 body unit | Each Squirrel body unit contributes optional Strained Carry                                    | Strained Cargo can be shed during Crossing                   |\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00102_6c044d0453aa",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3. Squirrel Trait: Strained Carry",
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "source_text": "<!--@3¶1-->\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td><strong>TRAIT SENTENCE<br />\n</strong>Each Squirrel body unit contributes 10 optional Strained Cargo slots to the party-wide inventory. Strained Cargo extends the haul but may be shed during Crossing.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00108_c25417c755af",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "list_item",
      "source_text": "  - Carry remains one party-wide inventory.\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00111_b7430ef059fd",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "list_item",
      "source_text": "  - Normal secured Carry is governed by the ordinary party rule.\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00114_a0c79d3e8ed3",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "list_item",
      "source_text": "  - Each Squirrel body unit adds 10 Strained slots to one shared Strained Inventory.\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00117_7a1a51a540ee",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "list_item",
      "source_text": "  - Guests do not add Strained capacity unless their own species trait later says otherwise.\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00122_93c1f09de4b1",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "table_row",
      "source_text": "| 3 Squirrel body units           | 30                         | 3                              |\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00123_a7c02de795dc",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "table_row",
      "source_text": "| 2 Squirrel body units + 1 Guest | 20                         | 2                              |\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00124_d214c4674e03",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "table_row",
      "source_text": "| 1 Squirrel body unit + 2 Guests | 10                         | 1                              |\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00125_3c4c02113452",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.1 Shared capacity",
      "block_type": "table_row",
      "source_text": "| No Squirrel body units          | 0                          | None                           |\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00189_3aebbe2262f3",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "3.5 Tuning status",
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "source_text": "<!--@3.5¶1-->\nThe 10 Strained slots per Squirrel body unit and 50% full-load ceiling are working values. The party-wide structure, proportional fill rule, one check per Squirrel per lane, random ordinary-Cargo loss, hidden execution, and Artifact exclusion are the more important architectural decisions.\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00246_3c4fef085254",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "5. Comparative Species Power",
      "block_type": "table_row",
      "source_text": "| Squirrel    | Optional shared Strained Carry                         | Secured Carry rules, party action economy, Artifact protection    | How much extra ordinary material is worth exposing to shedding?       |\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001__B00261_271ef1f94484",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CORE-TRAITS-001",
      "section": "6. Acceptance Tests",
      "block_type": "list_item",
      "source_text": "3.  A 2-Squirrel + 1-Guest party has one shared Strained Inventory with 20 slots and performs 2 hidden Jostle checks per crossed lane.\n"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CROSSING-001__LOCATION__10¶6",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CROSSING-001",
      "section": "10¶6",
      "block_type": "legacy_record",
      "source_text": "Squirrel Strained Carry is party-wide, pro-rated by Squirrel body units, and exposed to hidden lane-based Jostle checks."
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-CROSSING-001__LOCATION__6¶1",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-CROSSING-001",
      "section": "6¶1",
      "block_type": "legacy_record",
      "source_text": "Each Squirrel body unit contributes 10 slots to the party-wide Strained Inventory in addition to ordinary secured Carry."
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-HUMAN-RULINGS-001__LOCATION__L00202-L00212",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-HUMAN-RULINGS-001",
      "section": "L00202-L00212",
      "block_type": "legacy_record",
      "source_text": "Its all-caps operator is `RISK`. Its substantive MSID is `Away.Crossing`; Highway is its world manifestation."
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001__LOCATION__L00303-L00309",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001",
      "section": "L00303-L00309",
      "block_type": "legacy_record",
      "source_text": "Away.Crossing\nAway.Crossing.Phase\nAway.Crossing.Mouse\nAway.Crossing.Rabbit\nAway.Crossing.Squirrel"
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001__LOCATION__L00326-L00326",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001",
      "section": "L00326-L00326",
      "block_type": "legacy_record",
      "source_text": "The human-confirmed species branches must not be flattened into generic `Away.Crossing.Species.*` paths without adjudication."
    },
    {
      "block_key": "M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001__LOCATION__L00508-L00511",
      "source_id": "M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001",
      "section": "L00508-L00511",
      "block_type": "legacy_record",
      "source_text": "`Away.Crossing` is the substantive branch of the Crossing Register and is uniquely forked by Core Species."
    }
  ],
